**Definition 2.1 (physical correspondence).** All original CAP 0–63
ownership, origins and meanings are unchanged. In particular:

| Ports or resource | Actual use and admission |
| --- | --- |
| 0–12, 13, 16, 17 | Producer directory/work, retained ingress, original private arena and CAP descriptors; conversion obtains none of their live tokens. |
| 24/25/26/27 | Original table/state/acquired seed/waiting packet; 24/25/27 remain parked until 00. Initial owned import of 26 restores its head. |
| 28/29 | Acquired actor archive and ten-field CAP descriptors, imported only at the actual closed acquired boundaries, with head restoration. |
| 32–39, 40–47 | Occupied original verifier and consumer, including their actual descriptor grammars and terminal duties. |
| 48/49/50/51 | Original producer→actor, actor→producer, producer→verifier and verifier→consumer routes. |
| 64/65 | Alternating complete immutable word banks, both owned by $A$. |
| 66/67/68 | Native Base/ordinal scratch, length scratch and zero-based RCA descriptors. |
| 69/70 | Actual code capture/initial-prefix/staging, and retained outer/history ingress. |
| 71/72/73 | Immutable history archive/sender, history mailbox, history receiver. |
| History invocation slots | ARC's distinct outer-client and handler/client phase slots; every transfer is an actual TOK. |
| Mailbox availability/read slots | ARC's separate live availability and receiver-read resources; they are not identified with invocation or printed old tokens. |

CAP 17/29/33 descriptors are ten sep-delimited fields, seal, one-based
creation ordinals. RCA 68 descriptors have unary owner/port/base/length,
flags 10, zero-based ordinal, F and seal. Their equal numerals are not equal
origins. No compiler bank occupies verifier 33. Producer 1–12 transfer only
by the original twelve TOKs and final CTL when the original client resumes.
No added converter runs in a partial loan.

